.TH VACUUM 1 "November 2026" "Vacuum-IM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vacuum \- Jabber/XMPP instant messaging client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vacuum
.RB [ \-p
.IR profile ]
.RB [ \-pp
.IR password ]
.RB [ \-h
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR locale ]
.RB [ \-lt
.IR types ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Vacuum-IM
is a full-featured, cross-platform Jabber/XMPP client built with Qt. The
program itself is a plugin loader; all functionality, including multiple
accounts, multi-user chat, message history, file transfer, spell checking
and voice calls, is provided by plugins.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " profile"
Open the named profile.
.TP
.BI \-pp " password"
Password for the profile given with
.BR \-p .
Command-line arguments are visible to other local users, so avoid this
option on shared systems.
.TP
.BI \-h " directory"
Keep application data (profiles and settings) in
.I directory
instead of the default location.
.TP
.BI \-l " locale"
Use the given interface language, for example
.BR uk " or " de_DE .
.TP
.BI \-lt " types"
Enable logging of the given logger message types (a numeric mask).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/protomors/vacuum-im
